{"id":23534,"title":"A survey of modeling, rendering and animation of clouds in computer graphics","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00371-020-01953-y","final_url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s00371-020-01953-y.pdf","year":2020,"kind":"paper","source":"openalex","doi":"10.1007/s00371-020-01953-y","arxiv":null,"sha256":"a8324ba679ca65cb29c7af424fbff688aa50b6a5448099183a71cf18f49dd63c","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"oa","fetched_at":1793066437.8853614,"text_chars":89584,"abstract":"Abstract Clouds play an important role in enhancing the realism of outdoor scenes in computer graphics (CG). Realistic cloud generation is a challenging task, which entails processes such as modeling, photorealistic rendering and simulation of the clouds. To these ends, several techniques have been proposed within the CG community in the last 4 decades with one or more of the above stated focuses. The growth of modern hardware has also enabled development of techniques that can achieve cloud display and animation at interactive frame rates. In this survey, we review the prominent work in the domain and also summarize the evolution of the research over the time.","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s00371-020-01953-y.pdf","https://doi.org/10.1007/s00371-020-01953-y"],"cited_by":[{"path":"2190-volumetric-photon-mapping.md","name":"Volumetric Photon Mapping","k":2},{"path":"1053-single-scattering-model.md","name":"Single Scattering Model","k":2},{"path":"7049-radiance-predicting-neural-networks-rpnn.md","name":"Radiance-Predicting Neural Networks (RPNN)","k":1},{"path":"13472-general-fluid-simulation-update-loop.md","name":"General Fluid Simulation Update Loop","k":4},{"path":"15339-ray-marching-with-spherical-harmonics-sh-basis.md","name":"Ray Marching with Spherical Harmonics (SH) Basis","k":2},{"path":"14321-cinematic-quality-volumetric-clouds.md","name":"Cinematic Quality Volumetric Clouds","k":3},{"path":"15797-mie-phase-function-lookup.md","name":"Mie Phase Function Lookup","k":2},{"path":"16515-volumetric-cloud-rendering-with-pre-computed-light-transmitt.md","name":"Volumetric Cloud Rendering with Pre-computed Light Transmittance","k":2},{"path":"17619-navier-stokes-solvers.md","name":"Navier-Stokes Solvers","k":1},{"path":"15660-direct-sunlight-attenuation.md","name":"Direct Sunlight Attenuation","k":4},{"path":"6029-kajiya-von-herren-ray-tracing-algorithm.md","name":"Kajiya-Von Herren Ray Tracing Algorithm","k":2},{"path":"12488-scanline-a-buffer-rendering.md","name":"Scanline A-buffer rendering","k":1},{"path":"19855-cellular-automata-cloud-animation.md","name":"Cellular Automata Cloud Animation","k":1},{"path":"19856-particle-based-convective-cloud-simulation-neyret.md","name":"Particle-Based Convective Cloud Simulation (Neyret)","k":1},{"path":"19845-cloud-physics-temperature-and-buoyancy.md","name":"Cloud Physics: Temperature and Buoyancy","k":1},{"path":"19846-cloud-physics-humidity-and-saturation.md","name":"Cloud Physics: Humidity and Saturation","k":1},{"path":"19848-hybrid-physics-driven-procedural-model.md","name":"Hybrid Physics-Driven Procedural Model","k":1},{"path":"6212-physical-cloud-model-cumulus-convection.md","name":"Physical Cloud Model (Cumulus Convection)","k":2},{"path":"17236-data-pre-processing-for-animation.md","name":"Data Pre-processing for Animation","k":2},{"path":"2029-sabella-cloud-scattering.md","name":"Sabella Cloud Scattering","k":2},{"path":"12791-histogram-matching-for-parameter-optimization.md","name":"Histogram Matching for Parameter Optimization","k":2},{"path":"19871-lennard-james-potential-cloud-simulation.md","name":"Lennard-James Potential Cloud Simulation","k":1},{"path":"19067-atmospheric-scattering-models.md","name":"Atmospheric scattering models","k":2},{"path":"19892-texture-splatting.md","name":"Texture Splatting","k":2},{"path":"20165-flow-and-trajectory-visualization.md","name":"Flow and Trajectory Visualization","k":1}]}